# The coordinator waits a thousand times its Down bound before it re-places
# a down machine's roles: in practice it never re-places them. Since #909
# (oracles that do not judge) the heal oracle judges every seed from the
# audit's configuration in force, and excuses only a journal with a gone
# member on a seed whose Down bound reaches past its window. It still
# survives: every machine the sim takes down comes back in the tail and
# rejoins its journals in place, so a cell that never re-places heals all
# the same (600 seeds green on PR #925).
excuse: skip heal: re-place past tail
expect: survives #773
file: crates/lib/paros-coordinator/src/cell/watch.rs
--- find
        if now.saturating_sub(since) < self.replace_after {
--- replace
        if now.saturating_sub(since) < self.replace_after * 1000 {
--- end
